# WHAT: This file tells Git (the version control system) which files and
#       folders to IGNORE — meaning Git will not track them, show them in
#       "git status", or include them when you push code to GitHub.
#       These are files that are either temporary, generated at runtime, or
#       specific to your local computer and should not be shared.
# OPTIONS: Each line is a pattern. Git ignores any file/folder that matches.
#   - A plain name (e.g. __pycache__/) ignores folders with that exact name.
#   - A wildcard pattern (e.g. *.pyc) ignores all files ending in .pyc.
#   - A leading slash (e.g. /secrets.json) ignores only at the repo root.
#   - A trailing slash (e.g. logs/) means it is a directory.
# DEFAULTS: N/A (you must explicitly list what to ignore).
# OUTPUT/EFFECT: These files do not appear in "git status" and are not committed.
# ERRORS/EDGE CASES: If you accidentally add a pattern that matches source
#   code files, those files will be hidden from Git (dangerous!).
# HOW TO TEST: Run "git status" — ignored files should NOT appear in the output.
#               Run "git check-ignore -v <file>" to see which rule ignores a file.

# __pycache__/: Python's compiled bytecode cache folder (auto-generated, one per source file).
__pycache__/
# *.pyc: compiled Python bytecode files (auto-generated, can be re-created).
*.pyc
# .DS_Store: macOS folder metadata file (irrelevant on Linux, appears on every Mac).
.DS_Store
# *.log: log files produced by the app at runtime (grow over time, not code).
*.log
# .venv/: a local Python virtual environment folder (contains installed packages,
#   specific to this computer, should not be shared).
.venv/
# .pytest_cache/: pytest's temporary test cache folder (auto-generated, can be re-created).
.pytest_cache/
# .ruff_cache/: ruff linter's cache folder (auto-generated, can be re-created).
.ruff_cache/

# GUI contract test artifacts

## Launcher
GUI-SCRIPT-LAUNCHER/__pycache__/

## Test run caches
GUI-SCRIPT-LAUNCHER/files/__pycache__/
